{
  "id": "halden-power-complex",
  "title": "Halden four-unit power complex",
  "description": "Four independently simulated PWR units supply a dedicated 420 kV switchyard in the Norwegian transmission grid. Plant output and station-service demand participate directly in grid balance, flow, voltage, and frequency. Local weather evolves from rain through freezing conditions to clearing, with recorded ground probes. Weather is observable context; it does not yet change Plant or Grid physics.",
  "objectives": [
    "Operate four independent PWR units while monitoring their combined effect on the transmission grid.",
    "Observe actual grid frequency, reserve, voltage, and branch-flow response when a unit changes output or trips.",
    "Maintain offsite station-service power from the connected grid.",
    "Inspect local weather and persistent ground conditions at the complex and compare with the northern probe. Weather does not automatically cause equipment failures."
  ],
